WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.200
Here's how to run your first project on BuildPanda, in
ten simple steps.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.217
Step one. Create your account.

00:00:07.217 --> 00:00:10.900
Sign up in seconds, and you're ready to set up your
first build.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.819
Step two. Your dashboard.

00:00:13.819 --> 00:00:18.433
Every active project, its progress, and what needs you
today, all in one place.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.363
Step three. Open a project and it's ready from day one.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:27.600
Budget, phases, and milestones, built for you from your
schedule and bill of quantities.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.924
Step four. Always know what's next.

00:00:30.924 --> 00:00:35.233
The work that needs your attention is surfaced before it
has a chance to slip.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.313
Step five. Plan the work on a board.

00:00:39.313 --> 00:00:43.033
Organise tasks and subtasks, and move them across as the
build progresses.

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:46.522
Step six. See the whole programme.

00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:50.300
Your schedule as a Gantt chart, with dependencies and
the critical path.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.392
Step seven. Track your materials.

00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:57.867
Work straight from the bill of quantities as items are
ordered and used on site.

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.633
Step eight. Raise and track R F Is.

00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:05.967
Log a question, route it to the right person, and keep
every answer on the record.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.827
Step nine. Open the B I M model.

00:01:09.827 --> 00:01:13.500
View the federated model, select any element, and assign
it to a person.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.244
Step ten. Keep your client in the loop.

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:21.533
They see real progress and where the budget goes, so the
questions stop coming to you.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:23.761
That's it.

00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:26.900
Set up your first project today, at buildpanda dot io.
